  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image-only, singleprofile, resnet50) is much weaker at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The key uncertainty is whether moving from singleprofile to multiprofile (with aggregation) meaningfully improves RNA representation. config_002 tests exactly this: it is the minimal change from config_001 (singleprofile → multiprofile + avgpool), isolating the effect of multi-profile aggregation. This is the best next experiment because (1) it directly ablates a design axis that pervades the entire configuration space—knowing whether multiprofile helps determines whether to invest future budget in multiprofile multimodal configs or stick with singleprofile, (2) avgpool is the simplest aggregation, giving a clean signal before trying transformer, and (3) it reduces uncertainty about a high-leverage decision before committing to more complex multimodal experiments."
}

